.TH PLUGIN-QUALIFICATION-DB-WRITE 1 2026-11-19 plugin-db-qualification "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-qualification-db-write \- put and delete records in the OpenMixer qualification store's layers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-qualification-db-write put \-\-scope
.IR user | system
.B \-\-offer
.I word
.B \-\-host\-class
.I word
.RB [ \-\-contract\-dir
.IR dir ]
.br
.B plugin-qualification-db-write delete \-\-scope
.IR user | system
.B \-\-sha256
.I hash
.B \-\-format
.I format
.B \-\-uri
.I uri
.B \-\-offer
.I word
.B \-\-host\-class
.I word
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B put
reads one qualification record, the JSON document of plugin-qualify.qualification-record/1, on standard input and
replaces, whole and in one transaction, the layer's record of the same key (sha256, format, uri, offer, host class). The
layer is created from the installed DDL when its file is absent. Every word is checked against the contract domains;
the binary's path must be relative to the install root, its file list ordered, unique and not empty, and the key's
SHA-256 the one of the entry at that path.
.PP
.B delete
removes the layer's record of a key; a key the layer does not hold is not an error. Nothing is deleted from the base.
.PP
The user scope's layer is ~/.local/share/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite, the system scope's
/var/lib/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite. The contract directory is \-\-contract\-dir, then OMX_CONTRACT_PATH,
then the contractdir of libomx-domain.pc.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. A refusal is printed on standard error as
.I plugin-qualification-db-write: refused: name: ...
and exits 1: path-absolute, binary-not-in-files, key-not-the-binary, files-unordered, files-duplicate, files-empty,
word-unknown, field-unmapped, schema-refused, among others. A usage error exits 2.
